A||||6||ounmongk||my poor engine.||||9||
Z||000000||ounmongk||01-02-2000||08:01 PM||||well guys, this one's a doozy. I was driving on a county parkway today and suddenly I heard some noise coming from the engine. Sounded like someone was popping corn back there.  I almost made it home when I heard noises that sounded like popping corn or something. I'm not a gear-head, so bear with me now.. I think it was the drive belt that broke. (the belt the runs the alternator and I guess the water pump and some other stuff.) I tried to make it home, which was a mile away, but then the battery light came on, and then the thermostat light, and eventually the service engine soon light came on. when the engine started smoking,I stopped the car. is this devestating to the engine? because I found that it's possible the engine block could crack when it overheats too much... on that note, I need some companies of which I can get a reman. or recon. engine from. Thanks guys.||||reg||9
Z||000001||daved||01-02-2000||10:15 PM||||Look on the bright side; at least you stopped the engine before it siezed!  While the belt is off, reach down and turn the waterpump shaft and alternator shaft. If they turn alright, with no slop or grinding, then maybe all that happened is the belt shredded, and the popcorn effect was the pieces flying off. If so, it will be a cheap fix.  Good luck, Dave||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||01-03-2000||12:53 AM||||What motor? The four or the six? and it is the crank pully you will also need to turn.With a ratchet and socket||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||01-03-2000||02:05 AM||||I had a belt broke on me, i drove the car at least 2 miles, to get the the parts store near my house.  My car runs fine.  Its a 2.5L 84' fiero.  As long as you had oil in the car, you should be fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smokey||01-03-2000||03:18 AM||||fiero speeder is right. overheating is a common problem amoung many people. as long as you had the right amount of oil in it, i wouldn't be going and investing in a new engine already||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||01-03-2000||05:11 AM||||Amazingly, this very thing happened to another forum member recently.  His car ('87 coupe, I think) is still sitting waiting on the "right" belt.  He'll tell you more once he gets on line today.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ounmongk||01-03-2000||09:20 PM||||turns out the pulleys were misaligned, and that caused the belt to fly off and shred. wonder what caused that?!?||||reg||1
